  {
   "id": "p3",
   "text": "To answer it we built a small tool environment with three domains: a warehouse, a meeting calendar, and a support ticket queue. An agent runs scripted sessions of six to thirty tool calls. Some steps are questions it must answer from what it has already seen, with tools switched off. In a trap step, a superseded value is sitting in the context when the question arrives. In a neutral step, nothing competes.",
