  {
   "id": "p6",
   "text": "First result, on Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite over one hundred and forty-four episodes. Own updates never fail: all four layouts score one hundred percent. Neutral steps never fail either. The whole effect lives in external updates. There, the cache-optimal layout answers correctly sixty-five percent of the time. The pruned layout answers correctly ninety-six percent of the time. Reordering barely helps: seventy percent. The note recovers about a quarter of the gap: seventy-three percent.",
